This repository contains Persona-Pruner pruning and evaluation utilities.

The persona evaluation pipeline and data format are adapted from the Persona Vectors repository:
https://github.com/safety-research/persona_vectors

The OpenAI log-probability judge protocol follows the Persona Vectors evaluation setup, which itself
credits the Emergent Misalignment codebase for judge functions.

The generic instruction/answer source used for paper experiments was preprocessed from data released
with Few-Shot Preference Optimization (FSPO), including:
https://github.com/Asap7772/fewshot-preference-optimization
https://huggingface.co/datasets/sher222/persona-iterative-responses

This repository references those sources for provenance but does not redistribute their full dataset.

The vLLM rewrite generator is a cleaned, self-contained version of the local `akinator_may`
`inference_alpaca.py` workflow used for the paper's persona answer rewrites.

Large model checkpoints, training artifacts, and private experiment outputs are intentionally not
included in this source release.
